From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:06:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/29] payloads/external/edk2: Don't set
 PcdCapsuleOnDiskConnectBootDevice

Commit a2b77d9b03 ("payloads/external/edk2: Connect boot device for
disk capsules") sets this PCD with capsule-on-disk support, but
MrChromebox's EDK2 doesn't define it, so the payload build fails with
"The Pcd ... is not found in the DEC file".

Don't set it. MrChromebox's capsule-on-disk code still connects the
device path of the active boot option to find the ESP, which works when
that option names a file on the ESP, as installed bootloaders do.

MrChromebox's EDK2 needs "UefiPayloadPkg: Connect the disks before
processing capsules on disk" instead. Drop both once it defines the PCD.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 payloads/external/edk2/Makefile | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/payloads/external/edk2/Makefile b/payloads/external/edk2/Makefile
index 768bce5320..7515db5ec9 100644
--- a/payloads/external/edk2/Makefile
+++ b/payloads/external/edk2/Makefile
@@ -152,7 +152,6 @@ BUILD_STR += --pcd gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCapsuleEmbeddedDriverSuppor
 endif
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_DRIVERS_EFI_CAPSULE_ON_DISK_SUPPORT),y)
 BUILD_STR += --pcd gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCapsuleOnDiskSupport=TRUE
-BUILD_STR += --pcd gEfiMdeModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCapsuleOnDiskConnectBootDevice=TRUE
 endif
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_DRIVERS_EFI_CAPSULE_EMBED_FMP_DXE),y)
 BUILD_STR += -D CAPSULE_EMBED_FMP_DXE=TRUE
